{"id":"d092bc2753a71d25","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-thm-feit-thompson.md","title":"Feit–Thompson Theorem","display":"thm-feit-thompson — Feit–Thompson Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-feit-thompson","aliases":["58-thm-feit-thompson"],"display":"thm-feit-thompson — Feit–Thompson Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]","[[../batch01/58-df-commutator.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-feit-thompson"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-feit-thompson</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-feit-thompson — Feit–Thompson Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-group.md\">../batch09/58-df-group.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c94deae06f4e9873\" href=\"?note=c94deae06f4e9873\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-commutator.md\">../batch01/58-df-commutator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d740d724737a15d5\" href=\"?note=d740d724737a15d5\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md\">../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G,\\cdot,e,D,c,x,y\\in V\">\\(G,\\cdot,e,D,c,x,y\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Group}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Group}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-group.md\">../batch09/58-df-group.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Commutator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Commutator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"c94deae06f4e9873\" href=\"?note=c94deae06f4e9873\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-commutator.md\">../batch01/58-df-commutator.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d740d724737a15d5\" href=\"?note=d740d724737a15d5\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md\">../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}feit\\text{-}thompson}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot)\\land\\exists k\\in\\omega\\;(|G|=2k+1)\n\\to\n\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists D,e\\in V\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(D,n+1,\\mathcal P(G))\n\\land D(0)=G\n\\land D(n)=\\{e\\}\n\\land\\forall z\\in G\\;(e\\cdot z=z\\land z\\cdot e=z)\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\Bigl(D(i+1)\\subseteq D(i)\\land\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S(D(i+1),G,\\cdot)\\land\\forall x,y\\in D(i)\\;\\exists c\\in D(i+1)\\;\\mathrm{Commutator}_S(c,x,y,G,\\cdot)\\Bigr)\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}feit\\text{-}thompson}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot)\\land\\exists k\\in\\omega\\;(|G|=2k+1)\n\\to\n\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists D,e\\in V\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(D,n+1,\\mathcal P(G))\n\\land D(0)=G\n\\land D(n)=\\{e\\}\n\\land\\forall z\\in G\\;(e\\cdot z=z\\land z\\cdot e=z)\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\Bigl(D(i+1)\\subseteq D(i)\\land\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S(D(i+1),G,\\cdot)\\land\\forall x,y\\in D(i)\\;\\exists c\\in D(i+1)\\;\\mathrm{Commutator}_S(c,x,y,G,\\cdot)\\Bigr)\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Feit–Thompson (published 1963): every finite group of odd order is solvable.</li>\n<li>Used local group theory and character theory.</li>\n<li>Computer-assisted proof (2013): formalized in Coq by Gonthier et al.</li>\n<li>The theorem is a foundational input to the classification of finite simple groups, not a corollary normally derived from it.</li>\n<li>It extends solvability far beyond the orders covered by Burnside's <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p^a q^b\">\\(p^a q^b\\)</span> theorem.</li>\n<li>The operation is explicit. The finite normal series has every commutator of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D(i)\">\\(D(i)\\)</span> in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D(i+1)\">\\(D(i+1)\\)</span>, the abelian-factor characterization of solvability.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed71f39f59370734","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-commutator.md","status":"resolved","id":"c94deae06f4e9873","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-commutator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md","status":"resolved","id":"d740d724737a15d5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed71f39f59370734","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Group}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch09/58-df-group.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-commutator.md","status":"resolved","id":"c94deae06f4e9873","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Commutator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch01/58-df-commutator.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md","status":"resolved","id":"d740d724737a15d5","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch02/58-df-normal-subgroup.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"G,\\cdot,e,D,c,x,y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Group}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Commutator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}feit\\text{-}thompson}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,\\cdot)\\land\\exists k\\in\\omega\\;(|G|=2k+1)\n\\to\n\\exists n\\in\\omega\\;\\exists D,e\\in V\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(D,n+1,\\mathcal P(G))\n\\land D(0)=G\n\\land D(n)=\\{e\\}\n\\land\\forall z\\in G\\;(e\\cdot z=z\\land z\\cdot e=z)\n\\land\\forall i\\in n\\;\\Bigl(D(i+1)\\subseteq D(i)\\land\\mathrm{NormalSubgroup}_S(D(i+1),G,\\cdot)\\land\\forall x,y\\in D(i)\\;\\exists c\\in D(i+1)\\;\\mathrm{Commutator}_S(c,x,y,G,\\cdot)\\Bigr)\n\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"p^a q^b","display":false},{"tex":"D(i)","display":false},{"tex":"D(i+1)","display":false}],"bytes":1876,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4143","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-thm-feit-thompson.md|58-thm-feit-thompson]]（batch08）"}],"outgoing":["ed71f39f59370734","c94deae06f4e9873","d740d724737a15d5","36d7463d215be751"]}